    <title>Industry-Neutral Momentum and the Cross-Section of
  Expected Stock Returns</title>
    <summary>  We study a momentum signal that ranks stocks on their past twelve-month
return, skipping the most recent month, after removing the industry component of
returns. Industry-neutral momentum earns 0.92% per month (t = 4.1) in US common
stocks from 1965 to 2024 and is less exposed to momentum crashes than the raw
signal.
</summary>
